Original commit body from d2990e79097017fa7e73ffae405f19a51db9e6a1:

A declared axis (ADR-0024) stops a new SPELLING. Its registry and drift
linter reject an unregistered literal. Nothing ran an axiom's own sentence
against what the tool emits, so meaning drift went unseen: ADR-0050's medium
reading, ADR-0041's frame, Pony's computed kinds. This commit classifies
every declared axiom and tests each testable consequence through the
production pipeline.

docs/surveys/axiom-falsifiability.md classifies all 19 axioms:
- the 14 `_known_axes()` entries;
- ADR-0039, ADR-0041 (tier; directness/ecosystem) and ADR-0061;
- the verify-claims choice-shaped-source rule.
Each is mechanically testable, partly testable, or needs per-row judgment,
with the reason. For the judgment axioms (the ADR-0050 primary, ADR-0028's
"pathway", ADR-0051 owner paths, ADR-0039 calibration, a silence reason's
truth) it records what a reviewer samples instead. Existing meaning tests
are cited rather than duplicated: the edge-type runtime-coherence ratchet,
the ADR-0059 shrink-only ledger, INV-kutub's tier test, ADR-0058's consumer
scan, and ADR-0061 rulings 3/4/6.

New tests, lang-mainstream test_axiom_falsification.py, 80 pass + 17 xfail.
Fixtures go through run_behavior_map / cmd_verify_claims.

