Each test first asserts that its fixture reached what it tests. Each
property is one pure checker, with a hand-built counterexample in-suite.
The visibility failures: java package-private, csharp default-private
members and rust non-pub all read `public`, and the typescript `private` /
`protected` keywords are never read.

Mutation controls. Eight mutations were applied in a detached worktree with
a pinned PYTHONPATH (43 tests went red):

| # | Mutation | Tests that went red |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | visibility default -> private | every default row; the WI-gisip rows XPASSed |
| 2 | every post-pass gets a reason | silence, 16 surveys |
| 3 | no directness stamp | imported-stamp test |
| 4 | the shared unresolved emitter says ast_call | java, php, ts; the 8 WI-sukug rows XPASSed. Python has its own emitter and stayed green |
| 5 | .ts reads javascript | language, 2 TS surveys |
| 6 | java keys a lower-case receiver by its name | java module key |
| 7 | enrichment rewrites kind to route | py/java kind tests. TS's concept is analyzer-stamped and stayed green |
| 8 | a command-line catalogue is listed twice | tier-once |

The checker controls and both verify-claims reach controls stayed green.

